@anon.152f57749fcdf0a673d809c4f4545e7f.727 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [528 x i8] }> <{ [528 x i8] c"A supplement for the reference.\0A\0AFor references to headings or figures, this is added before the\0Areferenced number. For citations, this can be used to add a page number.\0A\0AIf a function is specified, it is passed the referenced element and\0Ashould return content.\0A\0A```example\0A#set heading(numbering: \221.\22)\0A#set ref(supplement: it => {\0A  if it.func() == heading {\0A    \22Chapter\22\0A  } else {\0A    \22Thing\22\0A  }\0A})\0A\0A= Introduction <intro>\0AIn @intro, we see how to turn\0ASections into Chapters. And\0Ain @intro[Part], it is done\0Amanually.\0A```" }>, align 1
